From: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: dwc3-msm: propagate the vbus change in dr_mode=peripheral

The state machine (dwc3_ext_event_notify: B_SESS_VLD) is only re-evaluated if
resume_work is queued, and the vbus_notifier only did it for dr_mode=OTG.
In dr_mode=peripheral the extcon updated vbus_active but the controller did not
enter LPM on disconnect: the 4e00000.hsusb wakeup source stayed active
(active_count=1 since boot) and autosleep never suspended.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
Signed-off-by: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
---

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c
@@ -4678,7 +4678,11 @@
 	}
 
 	mdwc->ext_idx = enb->idx;
-	if (mdwc->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_OTG && !mdwc->in_restart)
+	/* dace: in dr_mode=peripheral the state machine (B_SESS_VLD) must also
+	 * be re-evaluated when vbus changes, or on unplugging the cable the
+	 * controller does not enter LPM, the wakeup source stays active and
+	 * blocks autosleep. resume_work -> dwc3_ext_event_notify -> sm_work. */
+	if (!mdwc->in_restart)
 		queue_work(mdwc->dwc3_wq, &mdwc->resume_work);
 
 	return NOTIFY_DONE;
